        "file": "retry.py",
        "claim": "`attempts` is used directly in `range(attempts)` after only checking `attempts < 1`. Non-integer numeric values such as `3.0` or `3.5` will raise `TypeError` from `range` rather than a clear `ValueError`, and the docstring\u2019s \u201cat most `attempts` calls\u201d contract implies an integer call count.",
